### Is this a duplicate?

- [x] I searched existing CCCL issues and did not find this exact failure.

This may be architecturally related to #8534, but it is not the same reproducer: #8534 involves `cooperative_groups::thread_block::sync()` and CUDA 13.2. This report reproduces through CUB/Thrust scan-by-key with CUDA 12.9; the relevant `BlockScanWarpScans` path already uses `__syncthreads()`.

### Type of Bug

Silent Failure

### Component

CUB

### Describe the bug

On an RTX PRO 4500 Blackwell GPU (SM120), an exclusive scan-by-key silently returns incorrect results when all of the following are combined:

* CUDA Toolkit 12.9.86
* materialized contiguous key/value inputs (`int32_t*` / `size_t*`)
* a `cuda::tabulate_output_iterator`
* an output callback whose index argument is `int32_t`

The first output tile is correct. In the final partial tile, corruption begins at item 3150. The SM100/SM120 policy processes 3136 items per tile (224 threads x 14 items); item 3150 is `3136 + 14`. Beginning there, groups of 14 outputs contain thread-local prefixes but are missing the preceding-tile prefix. This is deterministic in the reproducer below.

The same source and current CCCL `main` pass when compiled with CUDA 13.3.33. With CUDA 12.9, three closely related control combinations pass:

| Input | Output | CUDA 12.9 / SM120 |
|---|---|---|
| contiguous | contiguous | pass |
| transform iterator | contiguous | pass |
| transform iterator | tabulate (`int32_t` index) | pass |
| contiguous | tabulate (`int32_t` index) | **fail: 59 mismatches** |

Changing only the tabulate callback index parameter from `int32_t` to `std::ptrdiff_t` also makes the failure disappear. There is no integer narrowing or overflow at the failing index. This looks like an iterator/type-dependent CUDA 12.9 code-generation or synchronization problem in the CUB scan path, rather than invalid 32-bit indexing.

I confirmed the failure both with CCCL 3.4.3 at `9d65c77f` (the version embedded in the application build where this was discovered) and with current CCCL `main` at `e63e44408b7ed198cd9c3fc88aceeb07ac77f1ca` (`v3.6.0.dev-308-ge63e44408`).

#### How this was found

This was reduced from four GPU Parquet failures in [NVIDIA/cudf-spark#15872](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cudf-spark/issues/15872) at cudf-spark merge commit `cf653a6` (PR parent `f5672773963`). Both dictionary and plain tiny-page Parquet variants, with native and Java footer configurations, failed with negative string sizes observed as `NegativeArraySizeException` near `ai.rapids.cudf.HostColumnVectorCore.getUTF8`.

The Jenkins CUDA 12 JNI artifact was `spark-rapids-jni-26.10.0-20260901.042007-20-cuda12.jar`, containing cuDF revision `299a974a23e402d8c6744c3ba699e145c16c6dbd`. The failure reproduced locally on the same GPU architecture and that exact cuDF revision with CUDA 12.9, but passed with CUDA 13.3.

The relevant cuDF operation is [the Parquet page string-offset scan](https://github.com/rapidsai/cudf/blob/299a974a23e402d8c6744c3ba699e145c16c6dbd/cpp/src/io/parquet/reader_impl_preprocess.cu#L1177-L1196). It materializes page keys and string byte counts, then performs `thrust::exclusive_scan_by_key` into a tabulate output iterator that writes `PageInfo::str_offset` using a `cudf::size_type` (`int32_t`) index.

Reduction observations from the real Parquet input:

* Plain file: 3209 pages, 59 incorrect offsets, first mismatch at item 3150 (`actual=832`, `expected=54888`).
* Dictionary file: 3215 pages, 65 incorrect offsets.
* Scanning into a contiguous `size_t` output produces zero mismatches.
* Copying that correct contiguous result separately into the identical tabulate destination produces zero mismatches and the full JNI read passes.
* Materializing transform-iterator inputs before the scan does not fix the original combined scan/output operation.
* Forcing CUDA 12 PTX instead of SASS still fails; the CUDA 13 build passes.

The standalone reproducer preserves only the relevant 176-byte output stride/member offsets, page counts, value pattern, iterator combinations, and callback index type. It has no cuDF, Spark, JNI, Parquet, or other RAPIDS dependency.

The cuDF revision already includes the earlier synchronization change from rapidsai/cudf#22152 (`block.sync()` to `__syncthreads()`), so that fix alone does not cover this case.

### How to Reproduce

Save this as `scan_by_key_sm120_repro.cu`:

```cuda
#include <cuda/iterator>
#include <cuda_runtime.h>

#include <thrust/device_vector.h>
#include <thrust/host_vector.h>
#include <thrust/scan.h>
#include <thrust/system/cuda/execution_policy.h>

#include <array>
#include <cstddef>
#include <cstdint>
#include <cstdio>
#include <cstdlib>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <string>
#include <vector>

namespace {

struct alignas(8) page_info {
  std::uint8_t page_data[8]{};
  std::size_t str_offset{};
  std::uint8_t before_chunk_idx[92]{};
  std::int32_t chunk_idx{};
  std::int32_t key{};
  std::uint8_t before_str_bytes[8]{};
  std::int32_t str_bytes{};
  std::uint8_t before_flags[25]{};
  std::uint8_t flags{};
  std::uint8_t suffix[22]{};
};

static_assert(sizeof(page_info) == 176);
static_assert(offsetof(page_info, str_offset) == 8);
static_assert(offsetof(page_info, key) == 112);
static_assert(offsetof(page_info, str_bytes) == 124);

struct get_key {
  __device__ std::int32_t operator()(page_info const& page) const { return page.key; }
};

struct get_value {
  __device__ std::size_t operator()(page_info const& page) const { return page.str_bytes; }
};

struct set_offset {
  page_info* pages;
  __device__ constexpr void operator()(std::int32_t i, std::size_t value) const
  {
    pages[i].str_offset = value;
  }
};

void check_cuda(cudaError_t status, char const* operation)
{
  if (status != cudaSuccess) {
    throw std::runtime_error(std::string(operation) + ": " + cudaGetErrorString(status));
  }
}

std::vector<page_info> make_pages()
{
  constexpr std::array<int, 7> preceding_page_counts{325, 82, 325, 325, 325, 528, 325};
  constexpr int date_pages = 974;
  std::vector<page_info> pages;
  pages.reserve(3209);
  for (std::size_t key = 0; key < preceding_page_counts.size(); ++key) {
    for (int i = 0; i < preceding_page_counts[key]; ++i) {
      page_info page{};
      page.key = static_cast<std::int32_t>(key);
      pages.push_back(page);
    }
  }
  for (int i = 0; i < date_pages; ++i) {
    page_info page{};
    page.key       = 9;
    page.str_bytes = i == date_pages - 1 ? 24 : (i % 12 == 0 ? 104 : 56);
    pages.push_back(page);
  }
  return pages;
}

template <typename Output>
bool validate(char const* mode, Output const& output, std::vector<page_info> const& input)
{
  std::size_t expected = 0;
  int mismatches       = 0;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < input.size(); ++i) {
    if (i == 0 || input[i].key != input[i - 1].key) { expected = 0; }
    auto const actual = output(i);
    if (actual != expected) {
      if (mismatches < 20) {
        std::printf("MISMATCH mode=%s item=%zu key=%d expected=%zu actual=%zu\n",
                    mode, i, input[i].key, expected, actual);
      }
      ++mismatches;
    }
    expected += input[i].str_bytes;
  }
  std::printf("RESULT mode=%s items=%zu mismatches=%d item3136=%zu item3150=%zu\n",
              mode, input.size(), mismatches, output(3136), output(3150));
  return mismatches == 0;
}

bool run_direct(std::vector<page_info> const& input)
{
  std::vector<std::int32_t> keys;
  std::vector<std::size_t> values;
  for (auto const& page : input) {
    keys.push_back(page.key);
    values.push_back(page.str_bytes);
  }
  thrust::device_vector<std::int32_t> d_keys(keys);
  thrust::device_vector<std::size_t> d_values(values);
  thrust::device_vector<std::size_t> d_output(input.size());
  thrust::exclusive_scan_by_key(thrust::cuda::par, d_keys.begin(), d_keys.end(),
                                d_values.begin(), d_output.begin());
  check_cuda(cudaDeviceSynchronize(), "direct scan synchronize");
  thrust::host_vector<std::size_t> output = d_output;
  return validate("direct-input-direct-output", [&](std::size_t i) { return output[i]; }, input);
}

bool run_transform_direct(std::vector<page_info> const& input)
{
  thrust::device_vector<page_info> pages(input);
  auto* begin = thrust::raw_pointer_cast(pages.data());
  auto keys   = cuda::transform_iterator(begin, get_key{});
  auto values = cuda::transform_iterator(begin, get_value{});
  thrust::device_vector<std::size_t> d_output(input.size());
  thrust::exclusive_scan_by_key(thrust::cuda::par, keys, keys + input.size(),
                                values, d_output.begin());
  check_cuda(cudaDeviceSynchronize(), "transform/direct scan synchronize");
  thrust::host_vector<std::size_t> output = d_output;
  return validate("transform-input-direct-output", [&](std::size_t i) { return output[i]; }, input);
}

bool run_transform_tabulate(std::vector<page_info> const& input)
{
  thrust::device_vector<page_info> pages(input);
  auto* begin = thrust::raw_pointer_cast(pages.data());
  auto keys   = cuda::transform_iterator(begin, get_key{});
  auto values = cuda::transform_iterator(begin, get_value{});
  auto output = cuda::make_tabulate_output_iterator(
    set_offset{thrust::raw_pointer_cast(pages.data())});
  thrust::exclusive_scan_by_key(thrust::cuda::par, keys, keys + input.size(), values, output);
  check_cuda(cudaDeviceSynchronize(), "transform/tabulate scan synchronize");
  thrust::host_vector<page_info> result = pages;
  return validate("transform-input-tabulate-output",
                  [&](std::size_t i) { return result[i].str_offset; }, input);
}

bool run_materialized_tabulate(std::vector<page_info> const& input)
{
  std::vector<std::int32_t> keys(input.size());
  std::vector<std::size_t> values(input.size());
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < input.size(); ++i) {
    keys[i]   = input[i].key;
    values[i] = input[i].str_bytes;
  }
  thrust::device_vector<std::int32_t> d_keys(keys);
  thrust::device_vector<std::size_t> d_values(values);
  thrust::device_vector<page_info> pages(input);
  auto* d_keys_ptr   = thrust::raw_pointer_cast(d_keys.data());
  auto* d_values_ptr = thrust::raw_pointer_cast(d_values.data());
  auto output = cuda::make_tabulate_output_iterator(
    set_offset{thrust::raw_pointer_cast(pages.data())});
  thrust::exclusive_scan_by_key(thrust::cuda::par, d_keys_ptr,
                                d_keys_ptr + input.size(), d_values_ptr, output);
  check_cuda(cudaDeviceSynchronize(), "materialized/tabulate scan synchronize");
  thrust::host_vector<page_info> result = pages;
  return validate("materialized-input-tabulate-output",
                  [&](std::size_t i) { return result[i].str_offset; }, input);
}

}  // namespace

int main()
{
  try {
    auto const input = make_pages();
    bool const ok = run_direct(input) && run_transform_direct(input) &&
                    run_transform_tabulate(input) && run_materialized_tabulate(input);
    if (!ok) { return EXIT_FAILURE; }
    std::printf("SCAN_BY_KEY_ITERATOR_PROBE_PASS\n");
    return EXIT_SUCCESS;
  } catch (std::exception const& error) {
    std::fprintf(stderr, "SCAN_BY_KEY_ITERATOR_PROBE_ERROR %s\n", error.what());
    return EXIT_FAILURE;
  }
}
```

From a CCCL checkout:

```bash
nvcc -std=c++17 -O3 -arch=native \
  -I./thrust -I./cub -I./libcudacxx/include \
  scan_by_key_sm120_repro.cu -o scan_by_key_sm120_repro
./scan_by_key_sm120_repro
```

CUDA 12.9.86 on current CCCL `main` produces:

```text
RESULT mode=direct-input-direct-output items=3209 mismatches=0 item3136=54104 item3150=54936
RESULT mode=transform-input-direct-output items=3209 mismatches=0 item3136=54104 item3150=54936
RESULT mode=transform-input-tabulate-output items=3209 mismatches=0 item3136=54104 item3150=54936
MISMATCH mode=materialized-input-tabulate-output item=3150 key=9 expected=54936 actual=832
MISMATCH mode=materialized-input-tabulate-output item=3151 key=9 expected=54992 actual=888
...
RESULT mode=materialized-input-tabulate-output items=3209 mismatches=59 item3136=54104 item3150=832
```

Compiling the identical source and identical CCCL commit with CUDA 13.3.33 produces zero mismatches in all four modes and prints `SCAN_BY_KEY_ITERATOR_PROBE_PASS`.

### Expected behavior

All iterator combinations should produce the same exclusive scan-by-key results. In particular, item 3150 should be `54936`, not `832`; changing a valid output callback index parameter from `int32_t` to `ptrdiff_t` should not change results within the `int32_t` range.

### Operating System

Ubuntu 24.04.4 LTS (Noble Numbat), x86_64. Host compiler: conda-forge GCC 13.4.0-20.

### nvidia-smi output

